            <div xml:id="d727">

                <pb facs="0741" n="643" sameAs="frus:frus1930v02/pg643"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">821.1561/89</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-03-28">March 28, 1930</date>.<lb/>[Received April
                        21.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1099</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to previous correspondence
                    concerning the objections of Grace and Company to a 25 per cent charge which had
                    been imposed on launch services in the port of Buenaventura, and with special
                    reference to my despatch No. 1056 of March 19, saying that I had taken up the
                    matter informally with the Colombian Minister of Foreign Affairs, I have the
                    honor to report that the Minister of Hacienda has signed a decree temporarily
                    lowering the tax on launches at Buenaventura from 25 to 15 per cent.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jefferson Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
